Subject: [PATCH 1/2] claude: Keep earlier quote levels in replies
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Cc: lab-devel@p7x.dev
Change-Id: wvotuklwpvtnoqrqwrxsznltvvnxxrum

Replies trimmed the quote to the lines they answered and dropped the
levels above them. An answer then sat under a question whose subject
had been cut, so the reader had to open earlier messages to learn
what was being discussed. That defeats the reason for working by
mail, where each reply carries the conversation with it.

State that trimming removes passages, not quote levels, and that each
message must make sense read alone.
---
change-id: wvotuklwpvtnoqrqwrxsznltvvnxxrum

 .claude/skills/process-email/SKILL.md |  7 ++++---
 CLAUDE.md                             | 14 +++++++++++---
 2 files changed, 15 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/.claude/skills/process-email/SKILL.md b/.claude/skills/process-email/SKILL.md
index 2bf352b..472c000 100644
--- a/.claude/skills/process-email/SKILL.md
+++ b/.claude/skills/process-email/SKILL.md
@@ -234,9 +234,10 @@ reply that leaves it out is lost to everyone else.
 
 Add a Message-ID header, e.g.
 `Message-ID: <$(date +%s).$(openssl rand -hex 6)@p7x.dev>`. Write the
-body by CLAUDE.md's quoting rules: trim the quote to what you answer,
-never reword it, and put each answer beneath the lines it answers.
-Wrap at 72.
+body by CLAUDE.md's quoting rules: trim the quote vertically to what
+you answer, keep every earlier quote level that gives it context, never
+reword it, and put each answer beneath the lines it answers. Wrap at
+72.
 
 If you posted a series, summarize what it does and cite it by its full
 subject with the Message-ID in a footnote, as CLAUDE.md describes, so
diff --git a/CLAUDE.md b/CLAUDE.md
index b4d76c5..8d769f1 100644
--- a/CLAUDE.md
+++ b/CLAUDE.md
@@ -85,9 +85,17 @@ client does. Do not paraphrase what someone wrote. Quote it.
 Open with an attribution line, e.g. "On <date>, <name> wrote:". Prefix
 every quoted line with "> ". Interleave your responses beneath the
 lines they answer, so the thread reads point then answer, top to
-bottom. Do not top-post. Trim the quote to the parts you actually
-answer, and never reword the text you keep. Your own words carry no
-"> " prefix.
+bottom. Do not top-post. Your own words carry no "> " prefix.
+
+Trim vertically, never horizontally. Cut the passages you do not
+answer, but keep every level of quoting above the lines you do
+answer: the question, and the earlier text the question was about.
+Never strip a whole indentation level. Mark a cut with "[...]" when
+it helps. Never reword the text you keep.
+
+Every message must read on its own. A reader who sees only your reply
+should know what each answer responds to, without opening another
+message. Keep enough of the earlier levels for that, and no more.
 
